35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found the budget is down a quarter, and a past joint clinic failed because neither side owned the rota. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The readmission drop was real but temporary. The booking system misses unbooked work entirely. We need to know what actually happened before adding more.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine unfilled nursing posts and rising agency costs. The therapy team is shrinking, though midwifery has slack. We need to balance this carefully.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is down a quarter, and off-site work earns nothing. We can only afford on-site programs that bill at standard rates.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The car park fills by eleven, and the shuttle misses most villages. If we add more, the whole system will seize up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that confirms my worry. If the budget shrinks, we can’t rely on outside partners. We need a program we fully control internally.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I agree. We must avoid repeating past failures. The data shows unbooked work vanishes, so we need a program with clear, trackable outcomes to ensure it actually helps patients.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, trackable outcomes are good, but they don’t fix empty beds. If we add work to already-broken rosters, the agency bill just climbs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, agency costs are a symptom, not the cause. If the program doesn’t generate revenue, we’re just buying expensive failure. Focus on the money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I hear you, but a full car park means patients simply can’t arrive. We must ensure the physical flow works before counting any revenue.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, you’re right. We can’t add strain to broken rosters. I’m looking for a program that strengthens our internal capacity without relying on fragile outside partnerships.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, I hear you. But if we don’t track the work, we can’t prove it helps. We need a program that fits within current staffing limits while remaining measurable.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the agency bill is the cause of the strain. If we ignore the staffing reality, the program fails before it starts.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, you’re confusing symptoms with the disease. If the program doesn’t pay for itself, the agency bill is irrelevant. We need self-sustaining revenue, not charity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I understand the strain. But if patients can’t reach the door, no amount of staffing helps. We must respect the physical limits.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I hear your urgency, but a program that ignores our staffing reality will collapse. We need something sustainable, not just profitable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, I understand the need for revenue. But without measurable patient benefit, we’re just adding noise. Let’s find a program that is both sustainable and actually helps people.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, I’m not ignoring the money. I’m saying the money is already gone to agency fees. We can’t bill for care we don’t have the staff to deliver.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, you’re hiding behind excuses. The ledger is clear: no revenue, no program. Stop complaining about staffing and start looking for a solution that pays.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, please be gentle. We are all tired. Let’s wait for the candidates to see if any fit our tight spaces and schedules.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
